WEBVTT

1
00:02:25.583 --> 00:02:26.625
Wait, wait.

2
00:02:39.042 --> 00:02:42.875
<i>We've got at least
16 guards on site, four vehicles primed.</i>

3
00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:45.917
Konrad's moving guns.

4
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.042
Lots of them.

5
00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:48.750
<i>He's a real piece of work.</i>

6
00:02:48.833 --> 00:02:51.958
He's up to his ears
in scanners and other jamming technology,

7
00:02:52.042 --> 00:02:54.333
so we're gonna lose comms
the moment we're inside.

8
00:02:54.417 --> 00:02:56.917
Question. Do we ever get any days off?

9
00:02:57.583 --> 00:03:00.583
- You're such a millennial, Nile.
- <i>Hey, it's a fair question.</i>

10
00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:03.417
Nile, we didn't have any days off

11
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.958
<i>when we were the new ones.</i>

12
00:03:05.042 --> 00:03:06.875
All right, Joe, Nicky,

13
00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:08.542
you guys take the hedge maze.

14
00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:11.333
What?

15
00:03:11.417 --> 00:03:12.667
Really?

16
00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.000
<i>Don't worry.</i>

17
00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:17.583
- It's not going to be like 1853.
- <i>What are you guys talking about?</i>

18
00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:19.208
There was a cannon.

19
00:03:19.292 --> 00:03:20.667
We didn't see it.

20
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.417
It was Booker.

21
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:28.458
His head was blown clean off by a cannon.
We couldn't find it in the maze.

22
00:03:28.542 --> 00:03:30.667
And he couldn't help, for obvious reasons.

23
00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.042
<i>You think he's okay?</i>

24
00:03:41.542 --> 00:03:42.792
Let's do this, guys.

25
00:03:44.042 --> 00:03:45.958
<i>Let us know if you put eyes on Konrad.</i>

26
00:03:46.042 --> 00:03:48.000
Two guards have moved to the waterfront.

27
00:03:48.083 --> 00:03:49.750
No sign of the big man yet.

28
00:03:53.542 --> 00:03:54.625
Hey.

29
00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:05.750
- He's only got one weapon.
- You sure?

30
00:04:06.333 --> 00:04:08.667
Do I need to remind you
you're not immortal?

31
00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:11.167
Fair enough.

32
00:04:38.833 --> 00:04:41.208
All right, guys. You know what to do.

33
00:04:41.792 --> 00:04:43.875
<i>Get as many guards
to chase you as you can.</i>

34
00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.500
<i>I make it look good</i>

35
00:04:49.583 --> 00:04:51.000
<i>I make it look easy…</i>

36
00:04:52.875 --> 00:04:55.000
- This one is mine!
- No, no, no!

37
00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:57.708
<i>I make it look good</i>

38
00:04:57.792 --> 00:05:00.000
<i>Last name, Danger</i>

39
00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:05.792
<i>Got a dead man on my back…</i>

40
00:05:05.875 --> 00:05:07.958
<i>It worked. They're heading your way.</i>

41
00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:15.292
They're supposed to follow us,
not to catch us.

42
00:05:22.875 --> 00:05:24.750
<i>I make it look easy…</i>

43
00:05:30.542 --> 00:05:31.958
All right. We're heading in.

44
00:05:33.375 --> 00:05:34.583
<i>Easy</i>

45
00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:35.792
<i>I make it look good</i>

46
00:05:47.542 --> 00:05:49.542
<i>I make it look good</i>

47
00:06:01.208 --> 00:06:02.917
What? No sex swing?

48
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.458
You must have seen some bad art
in your time, haven't you?

49
00:06:05.542 --> 00:06:08.292
This bad? Not in at least a century.

50
00:06:10.208 --> 00:06:11.708
Weapons being loaded.

51
00:06:13.417 --> 00:06:16.167
They're on the move.
Commotion must've spooked 'em.

52
00:06:48.417 --> 00:06:50.337
I need to remind you,
you're not immortal either.

53
00:06:52.208 --> 00:06:54.625
- Shall I?
- Nope. I always go first.

54
00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.167
Nicky.

55
00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.292
Slow down, Joe! Slow down!

56
00:07:41.667 --> 00:07:43.500
<i>Let's give these guys a run.</i>

57
00:08:00.625 --> 00:08:02.042
Ah shit!

58
00:08:38.125 --> 00:08:39.125
Fuck!

59
00:09:30.708 --> 00:09:32.333
Konrad's upstairs.

60
00:09:46.833 --> 00:09:48.208
Get in! Get in! Get in!

61
00:10:01.042 --> 00:10:02.125
Nicolò.

62
00:10:22.625 --> 00:10:24.208
- You okay?
- Yeah.

63
00:10:57.958 --> 00:11:00.500
- Move.
- Stay on my six.

64
00:11:06.167 --> 00:11:07.958
Sixteen guards, huh?

65
00:11:08.042 --> 00:11:10.625
Go easy.
CIA never taught him how to count.

66
00:11:10.708 --> 00:11:13.000
Can we just, you know, do this?

67
00:12:00.333 --> 00:12:01.333
Looks good on you.

68
00:12:20.375 --> 00:12:21.625
We're all set.

69
00:12:21.708 --> 00:12:24.458
My CIA contact will be here
in seven minutes.

70
00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:27.458
He'll make sure the weapons are collected.

71
00:12:27.542 --> 00:12:29.542
Okay, let's start walking.

72
00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.750
<i>Whoa! I'm a big bag hunter
With the bow</i>

73
00:12:34.833 --> 00:12:36.792
<i>She got a big bad dumper, drop it low</i>

74
00:12:36.875 --> 00:12:39.083
<i>Mama called me
And she happy with the grow</i>

75
00:12:39.167 --> 00:12:41.833
<i>Never ever fold for a thottie
That's an oath</i>

76
00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.250
Shh!

77
00:12:47.333 --> 00:12:48.625
You gonna call it?

78
00:12:49.542 --> 00:12:51.458
- I'm thinking.
- She has tells.

79
00:12:52.042 --> 00:12:53.917
Took me centuries to learn them.
She has tells.

80
00:12:56.292 --> 00:12:58.958
- No one can read Andy.
- No, I think I can.

81
00:12:59.042 --> 00:13:00.708
Yeah.

82
00:13:00.792 --> 00:13:02.208
- Yeah?
- Oh yeah.

83
00:13:04.333 --> 00:13:05.417
She's telling the truth.

84
00:13:06.583 --> 00:13:09.250
- Last two rounds.
- Her left eye twitched last two rounds.

85
00:13:10.542 --> 00:13:12.000
The left eye.

86
00:13:12.083 --> 00:13:13.125
What?

87
00:13:13.833 --> 00:13:15.625
- Bullshit.
- You sure?

88
00:13:16.958 --> 00:13:18.208
Bullshit.

89
00:13:24.583 --> 00:13:26.125
Thank you.

90
00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:30.375
You know the worst part
about being mortal?

91
00:13:31.708 --> 00:13:33.542
Just the fucking hangovers.

92
00:13:35.208 --> 00:13:38.042
Too brutal, man. I don't know.

93
00:13:38.125 --> 00:13:40.167
- What the...
- I don't know how you do it.

94
00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.250
Be right back.

95
00:13:42.958 --> 00:13:45.458
Whoo! The drinking is fun.

96
00:13:45.542 --> 00:13:47.417
- Who you texting?
- It's my new boyfriend.

97
00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:48.625
Come on. Let's go to bed.

98
00:13:51.042 --> 00:13:53.583
Sure, have another glass.

99
00:13:53.667 --> 00:13:55.958
You'll snore all night like a boar.

100
00:13:56.042 --> 00:13:57.167
Wow.

101
00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.833
You sleep talk all night.

102
00:13:59.917 --> 00:14:01.958
- <i>Ciao.</i>
- Good night.

103
00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.542
You did real good today.

104
00:14:06.625 --> 00:14:09.208
Even though I drove a boat
halfway into the villa?

105
00:14:09.292 --> 00:14:12.250
Hey, listen, sometimes quick
is better than subtle.

106
00:14:12.333 --> 00:14:14.292
Oh! Today's lesson?

107
00:14:14.792 --> 00:14:16.708
Yes, it is.

108
00:14:22.625 --> 00:14:24.458
You know, you joke a lot, but…

109
00:14:25.875 --> 00:14:26.917
How are you doing?

110
00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.000
Me?

111
00:14:30.625 --> 00:14:32.125
I'm really happy.

112
00:14:36.542 --> 00:14:37.667
I'm at peace.

113
00:14:40.458 --> 00:14:43.167
Didn't look peaceful when you were
throwing that guy out the window.

114
00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:44.833
It wasn't supposed to be.

115
00:14:45.875 --> 00:14:46.958
Send it now.

116
00:14:47.458 --> 00:14:50.417
I mean, I'm mortal. I'm not retired.

117
00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:53.542
My contact confirmed
that Konrad wasn't the buyer.

118
00:14:54.042 --> 00:14:56.958
Just a conduit,
like the others last month.

119
00:14:57.042 --> 00:14:59.917
So who is? And what are they doing
with all that artillery?

120
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.917
The real buyer is elusive.
Leaves almost no trace.

121
00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:06.458
This CCTV photo
is all they're able to get me.

122
00:15:07.208 --> 00:15:08.208
Hey.

123
00:15:10.958 --> 00:15:11.958
What?

124
00:15:14.667 --> 00:15:16.458
- You know this woman?
- Yeah.

125
00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:21.667
I mean no. No, I…

126
00:15:22.833 --> 00:15:24.667
I think I recognize her.

127
00:15:25.875 --> 00:15:27.667
I've dreamt about her.

128
00:15:28.333 --> 00:15:31.167
I didn't think it meant anything.
It wasn't clear.

129
00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:34.750
Okay, just… tell me exactly what you saw.

130
00:15:36.042 --> 00:15:37.375
This woman.

131
00:15:38.625 --> 00:15:39.958
She's, um…

132
00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:41.875
<i>She's in a room,</i>

133
00:15:41.958 --> 00:15:44.792
<i>an ancient room, surrounded by books.</i>

134
00:15:44.875 --> 00:15:46.917
<i>She's here, isn't she?</i>

135
00:15:51.625 --> 00:15:53.750
<i>And there's someone else there. A…</i>

136
00:15:54.458 --> 00:15:55.583
<i>A man, but…</i>

137
00:15:57.417 --> 00:15:59.208
<i>…I can't see his face.</i>

138
00:16:01.625 --> 00:16:04.500
<i>But the books, I think they're his.</i>

139
00:16:07.167 --> 00:16:09.542
<i>None of you had a choice.</i>

140
00:16:12.958 --> 00:16:14.875
<i>She's hurting him.</i>

141
00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:18.250
<i>And then…</i>

142
00:16:21.208 --> 00:16:22.292
<i>And then what?</i>

143
00:16:22.958 --> 00:16:24.458
<i>And then I wake up.</i>

144
00:16:27.708 --> 00:16:29.333
Think it means something?

145
00:16:30.208 --> 00:16:31.208
I don't know.

146
00:16:32.917 --> 00:16:35.542
There's not enough data yet
to get facial recognition,

147
00:16:35.625 --> 00:16:38.125
but the moment they do, I'll let you know.

148
00:16:38.208 --> 00:16:40.083
Great. Thanks, Copley.

149
00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:47.458
Hey. Don't worry about this, okay?

150
00:16:48.542 --> 00:16:49.750
We'll figure it out.

151
00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:14.833
Booker.

152
00:17:17.375 --> 00:17:19.500
It's nice to finally meet you.

153
00:17:28.792 --> 00:17:32.958
I've been waiting for a very long time.

154
00:17:34.958 --> 00:17:35.958
Quynh?

155
00:17:41.458 --> 00:17:42.458
So…

156
00:17:44.625 --> 00:17:46.875
How do I find Andromache?

157
00:18:14.625 --> 00:18:17.458
So, do you have any idea where we can go?

158
00:18:18.083 --> 00:18:20.250
I was thinking of having some time alone.

159
00:18:21.292 --> 00:18:22.292
Huh.

160
00:18:23.042 --> 00:18:24.833
Just a little time for myself.

161
00:18:26.333 --> 00:18:27.458
Okay.

162
00:18:27.542 --> 00:18:28.542
Thanks.

163
00:18:33.042 --> 00:18:34.458
You're coming with me.

164
00:18:35.292 --> 00:18:36.292
I am?

165
00:18:36.333 --> 00:18:37.667
I need your help.

166
00:18:41.208 --> 00:18:43.000
Try and have some fun without me.

167
00:18:43.083 --> 00:18:44.708
Bye, boss.

168
00:18:45.292 --> 00:18:46.292
Nile.

169
00:18:51.583 --> 00:18:52.833
Don't worry, okay?

170
00:18:54.167 --> 00:18:55.500
Enjoy yourself.

171
00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:14.792
What's up with Joe?
Did something happen after the wreck?

172
00:19:14.875 --> 00:19:17.167
He said he wanted some time alone.

173
00:19:19.375 --> 00:19:20.917
You're not okay with that?

174
00:19:23.833 --> 00:19:25.667
I know this man a thousand years.

175
00:19:26.875 --> 00:19:27.917
I know when he's lying.

176
00:19:34.958 --> 00:19:36.458
- Thank you.
- We're following him.

177
00:19:37.375 --> 00:19:38.375
What?

178
00:19:40.625 --> 00:19:41.625
Come on.

179
00:20:00.042 --> 00:20:03.875
Again, do you know where Andromache is?

180
00:20:05.583 --> 00:20:07.333
It doesn't matter if I do.

181
00:20:07.833 --> 00:20:09.292
I'm in exile.

182
00:20:10.167 --> 00:20:12.833
- But you can find her.
- Are you listening to what I say?

183
00:20:15.125 --> 00:20:16.750
I'm exiled.

184
00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:19.750
How'd you find me?

185
00:20:21.833 --> 00:20:23.125
You made it easy.

186
00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:26.500
Staggering around Paris drunk for months.

187
00:20:28.167 --> 00:20:30.417
It's a miracle you weren't discovered.

188
00:20:32.792 --> 00:20:34.958
So you bringing me here is…

189
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.625
Is you doing me a favor, right?

190
00:20:38.875 --> 00:20:40.250
Yeah.

191
00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:42.958
I'm sorry. I'm telling you the truth.

192
00:20:43.458 --> 00:20:44.583
I'm out of it.

193
00:20:45.083 --> 00:20:47.583
You wanna know where Andy is?
This is not the way to do it.

194
00:20:55.375 --> 00:20:56.458
He will need clean clothes.

195
00:21:13.042 --> 00:21:14.625
Has she spoken of me?

196
00:21:20.292 --> 00:21:21.625
She never stopped.

197
00:21:26.833 --> 00:21:28.542
All that time,

198
00:21:29.167 --> 00:21:31.500
with every last breath I took,

199
00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:35.167
I imagined she was trapped somewhere

200
00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:36.917
in the same hell as me.

201
00:21:38.875 --> 00:21:40.542
All I wanted

202
00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:45.458
was to get out and release her from it.

203
00:21:48.542 --> 00:21:50.333
Just to find out

204
00:21:50.417 --> 00:21:53.417
she'd been free for 500 years.

205
00:21:59.167 --> 00:22:01.833
She was living in her own kind of hell.

206
00:22:02.833 --> 00:22:05.000
Now, that's hard to believe.

207
00:22:22.208 --> 00:22:23.208
<i>Merci.</i>

208
00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:33.583
Not much of an exile

209
00:22:33.667 --> 00:22:35.958
if you're dropping in
to deliver groceries.

210
00:22:42.958 --> 00:22:44.125
Booker's alone.

211
00:22:45.667 --> 00:22:47.125
Nicky, <i>caro, </i>what…

212
00:22:47.667 --> 00:22:49.125
- He's alone.
- Yeah.

213
00:22:49.208 --> 00:22:51.042
And you were the one
screaming for his head.

214
00:22:51.125 --> 00:22:52.292
We abandoned him.

215
00:22:52.375 --> 00:22:53.833
He made his choice, Joe,

216
00:22:53.917 --> 00:22:56.458
when he shot Andy and betrayed all of us.

217
00:22:56.542 --> 00:22:58.958
Guys, something's happened. He's not here.

218
00:22:59.542 --> 00:23:01.458
There's blood on the wall,
blood on the floors.

219
00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:04.458
When is the last time you talked to him?

220
00:23:05.667 --> 00:23:08.167
- Joe.
- No reason in pretending now, Joe.

221
00:23:08.250 --> 00:23:09.875
I don't know. A week… a week ago.

222
00:23:09.958 --> 00:23:12.250
He was fine… I don't...

223
00:23:12.333 --> 00:23:14.750
We gotta tell Andy,
but it keeps going to voicemail.

224
00:23:15.333 --> 00:23:17.250
Come on. We'll meet them at Echo.

225
00:23:19.083 --> 00:23:20.958
- Nicky. Nicky!
- Come on. Come on.

226
00:23:28.250 --> 00:23:31.375
All this way, and you still
haven't told me who it is we're meeting.

227
00:23:32.792 --> 00:23:36.833
I made a promise the last time I saw him
that I would protect his secret.

228
00:23:38.458 --> 00:23:40.458
It's just around this corner here.

229
00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:44.583
Actually, I think maybe
I should just check in with him first.

230
00:23:44.667 --> 00:23:46.208
- Yeah.
- See if this is okay.

231
00:23:46.292 --> 00:23:48.208
Of course. I'll be on call.

232
00:23:48.750 --> 00:23:49.750
Okay.

233
00:24:25.375 --> 00:24:27.542
Andromache.

234
00:24:30.042 --> 00:24:31.042
You were expecting me?

235
00:24:32.708 --> 00:24:34.583
Let's just say I'm not surprised.

236
00:24:47.708 --> 00:24:48.792
Thank you.

237
00:24:58.833 --> 00:25:01.083
You're still wearing Quynh's necklace.

238
00:25:08.500 --> 00:25:10.042
Do you still dream about everyone?

239
00:25:11.917 --> 00:25:12.917
I keep tabs.

240
00:25:13.375 --> 00:25:16.208
- Do you know about Nile?
- Nile Freeman.

241
00:25:17.167 --> 00:25:18.167
I do.

242
00:25:18.208 --> 00:25:20.042
Well, she's been dreaming about a woman.

243
00:25:21.292 --> 00:25:23.583
A woman who was here with you.

244
00:25:24.083 --> 00:25:26.333
I thought maybe you'd know something.

245
00:25:29.417 --> 00:25:31.167
Why don't you come to the library?

246
00:25:33.583 --> 00:25:35.042
I think we should talk.

247
00:25:36.083 --> 00:25:37.500
So do I.

248
00:25:40.958 --> 00:25:45.250
You know, Tuah, I almost completely
stopped believing in our purpose

249
00:25:46.083 --> 00:25:48.958
until a friend of mine discovered
a ripple effect.

250
00:25:50.625 --> 00:25:51.833
Where's this friend?

251
00:25:53.167 --> 00:25:54.500
So, uh,

252
00:25:54.583 --> 00:25:55.917
how old are you, then?

253
00:25:57.417 --> 00:26:00.708
Let's just say 2,300 for a round number.

254
00:26:01.708 --> 00:26:02.708
You?

255
00:26:03.167 --> 00:26:04.250
I'm 43.

256
00:26:05.667 --> 00:26:06.667
Impressive.

257
00:26:28.125 --> 00:26:29.208
Uh…

258
00:26:34.250 --> 00:26:35.292
This is…

259
00:26:37.375 --> 00:26:39.917
All about immortals?

260
00:26:40.833 --> 00:26:43.792
Yes, our place in history.

261
00:26:43.875 --> 00:26:46.042
The facts and fictions
that have found their way

262
00:26:46.125 --> 00:26:48.083
into the writings of cultures

263
00:26:48.583 --> 00:26:52.125
and civilizations… the world over.

264
00:26:52.958 --> 00:26:55.208
Evidence of what you found out

265
00:26:55.292 --> 00:26:57.125
within 43 short years.

266
00:26:57.208 --> 00:26:58.625
Cause and effect.

267
00:26:59.125 --> 00:27:00.333
A life saved in Ghana…

268
00:27:01.125 --> 00:27:05.083
Leads to a Nobel Prize in medicine
three generations later.

269
00:27:06.375 --> 00:27:07.750
What happened over there?

270
00:27:09.917 --> 00:27:12.625
Those volumes were stolen by one of us.

271
00:27:16.917 --> 00:27:18.625
The woman Nile's been dreaming about?

272
00:27:21.500 --> 00:27:24.083
I've written books
on every single immortal.

273
00:27:24.167 --> 00:27:25.833
You, your friends, the work that they...

274
00:27:25.917 --> 00:27:27.375
Who is she, Tuah?

275
00:27:28.875 --> 00:27:31.125
She's gone by many names over the years.

276
00:27:31.208 --> 00:27:32.583
She goes by Discord now.

277
00:27:33.667 --> 00:27:34.750
Sounds ominous.

278
00:27:34.833 --> 00:27:35.958
As it should.

279
00:27:37.083 --> 00:27:38.958
She was the first of our kind
that I had met.

280
00:27:40.042 --> 00:27:41.250
A long time ago.

281
00:27:41.875 --> 00:27:43.042
How long?

282
00:27:44.958 --> 00:27:47.292
She is older than any of us.

283
00:27:49.750 --> 00:27:52.833
She is the first of the immortals.

284
00:27:52.917 --> 00:27:53.917
No.

285
00:27:54.250 --> 00:27:56.167
No, Andromache is the first.

286
00:27:59.583 --> 00:28:00.833
What are you saying?

287
00:28:00.917 --> 00:28:03.667
I… I… I found no trace of anyone earlier.

288
00:28:04.167 --> 00:28:06.333
- By design.
- What do you mean, "by design"?

289
00:28:07.500 --> 00:28:10.417
There was a time
where we walked together peacefully.

290
00:28:11.208 --> 00:28:12.917
But over the centuries,

291
00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.625
we saw how fear of those who are different

292
00:28:15.708 --> 00:28:18.333
can turn even good men cruel.

293
00:28:28.292 --> 00:28:29.750
We have to do something.

294
00:28:30.917 --> 00:28:31.917
They're like us.

295
00:28:32.417 --> 00:28:34.500
Please! No! No!

296
00:28:45.208 --> 00:28:48.208
Such evil cannot be unseen.

297
00:28:55.875 --> 00:28:58.542
No! No! No!

298
00:28:58.625 --> 00:28:59.958
Quynh!

299
00:29:00.042 --> 00:29:03.125
Quynh!

300
00:29:04.583 --> 00:29:06.375
That was the day you saved me.

301
00:29:06.958 --> 00:29:08.042
She was there too?

302
00:29:08.958 --> 00:29:09.958
Yes.

303
00:29:12.292 --> 00:29:16.500
Afterwards, I retreated
to my books, my research.

304
00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:18.542
And Discord retreated too.

305
00:29:19.125 --> 00:29:23.500
Then she spent the next five centuries
amassing untold wealth and power

306
00:29:24.250 --> 00:29:26.292
so as not to fear enemy or attack.

307
00:29:27.083 --> 00:29:29.167
Dealing arms with people like Konrad.

308
00:29:34.708 --> 00:29:36.875
What does she want from us, Tuah?

309
00:29:36.958 --> 00:29:37.958
I don't know.

310
00:29:38.042 --> 00:29:40.542
She's not the same person
that I once knew.

311
00:29:40.625 --> 00:29:44.250
And now that she knows your histories,
your relationships,

312
00:29:44.833 --> 00:29:47.958
I believe that all of you
could be in danger.

313
00:29:50.333 --> 00:29:52.500
It's been millennia
since I've been afraid.

314
00:29:53.708 --> 00:29:56.917
But I am scared of what she is capable of,

315
00:29:58.083 --> 00:29:59.458
and so should you.

316
00:30:05.667 --> 00:30:06.667
Tuah.

317
00:30:09.292 --> 00:30:11.292
Do you think there's a chance

318
00:30:12.500 --> 00:30:14.917
she might know
that I've lost my immortality?

319
00:30:17.625 --> 00:30:18.792
How long has it been?

320
00:30:21.750 --> 00:30:23.167
Around six months.

321
00:30:26.250 --> 00:30:27.542
Andromache.

322
00:30:31.125 --> 00:30:32.667
I think you should pack a bag.

323
00:30:33.750 --> 00:30:35.125
I already have.

324
00:30:38.417 --> 00:30:41.708
<i>Because I knew what you were gonna say.</i>

325
00:30:41.792 --> 00:30:43.833
No. You thought you knew what I'd say.

326
00:30:44.417 --> 00:30:45.583
You lied to us.

327
00:30:45.667 --> 00:30:46.792
They're back.

328
00:30:46.875 --> 00:30:48.625
- Hey.
- Hey.

329
00:30:50.042 --> 00:30:51.333
Who's this?

330
00:30:53.875 --> 00:30:56.542
This is Tuah, an old friend of mine.

331
00:30:56.625 --> 00:30:57.750
"An <i>old </i>friend"?

332
00:30:59.083 --> 00:31:01.458
You knew there was another,
and you never told us?

333
00:31:02.917 --> 00:31:04.625
Boss, you lied to us?

334
00:31:05.417 --> 00:31:06.250
I didn't lie. I...

335
00:31:06.333 --> 00:31:08.333
A lie of omission is still a lie.

336
00:31:08.833 --> 00:31:12.292
In Andromache's defense,
I asked her not to tell anyone of me.

337
00:31:13.917 --> 00:31:15.792
Something's happened to Booker.

338
00:31:16.542 --> 00:31:17.542
What?

339
00:31:20.333 --> 00:31:22.583
- Did you go see him?
- It's not like that.

340
00:31:25.042 --> 00:31:28.917
Yusuf went to see him.
They've been talking the entire time.

341
00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:31.833
- We went to his place in Paris.
- Blood everywhere.

342
00:31:33.583 --> 00:31:34.583
Discord.

343
00:31:36.167 --> 00:31:37.167
Possibly.

344
00:31:37.708 --> 00:31:40.917
What else do we know about her?

345
00:31:41.000 --> 00:31:43.167
I mean, where she lives, her…

346
00:31:43.875 --> 00:31:45.792
Her habits, her MO.

347
00:32:02.292 --> 00:32:03.292
It's Booker.

348
00:32:04.583 --> 00:32:06.833
Don't worry, boss. We got this.

349
00:32:08.833 --> 00:32:09.958
We have to.

350
00:32:33.417 --> 00:32:34.500
Thanks for coming.

351
00:32:38.333 --> 00:32:40.083
- Joe.
- Hey.

352
00:32:43.917 --> 00:32:45.208
- What happened?
- Hmm.

353
00:32:47.542 --> 00:32:49.125
I need to see Andy.

354
00:33:13.167 --> 00:33:14.167
Andy.

355
00:33:18.958 --> 00:33:20.208
She's out.

356
00:33:22.917 --> 00:33:23.917
What?

357
00:33:23.958 --> 00:33:25.167
Quynh.

358
00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:30.625
She couldn't find you, so she found me.

359
00:33:59.583 --> 00:34:01.000
<i>Andromache.</i>

360
00:34:02.375 --> 00:34:04.958
<i>I have returned to a world</i>

361
00:34:05.042 --> 00:34:08.875
<i>darker than the tomb I finally escaped,</i>

362
00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:15.292
<i>only to learn
you have gone on living in it freely</i>

363
00:34:16.083 --> 00:34:18.167
<i>all these centuries.</i>

364
00:34:19.875 --> 00:34:24.583
<i>I need to hear the words
that will free me from my true prison.</i>

365
00:34:27.250 --> 00:34:29.125
<i>That of a broken promise.</i>

366
00:34:29.917 --> 00:34:31.250
You and me.

367
00:34:32.750 --> 00:34:33.833
Until the end.

368
00:34:34.333 --> 00:34:36.917
<i>Find me where you always could.</i>

369
00:34:44.292 --> 00:34:45.625
I have to go meet her.

370
00:34:47.000 --> 00:34:49.417
- Andy, don't.
- It's Quynh.

371
00:34:53.500 --> 00:34:55.708
Give her space, Nile.

372
00:34:57.458 --> 00:35:00.375
Andy, she could have reached out to you
in a million ways.

373
00:35:00.458 --> 00:35:03.167
Instead, she kidnaps Booker
and does all this for face time?

374
00:35:03.250 --> 00:35:04.333
That seem sane to you?

375
00:35:04.417 --> 00:35:07.917
For 1,500 years, it was just her and me.
What do you know about her, Nile?

376
00:35:09.167 --> 00:35:12.000
I know you can die and I can't.

377
00:35:12.708 --> 00:35:15.208
And I know your head's not on straight
when it comes to her.

378
00:35:15.292 --> 00:35:18.792
So tell me, if our places were swapped,
would you let me go alone?

379
00:35:29.792 --> 00:35:31.542
So I guess you must be, uh,

380
00:35:32.667 --> 00:35:33.667
Tuah, right?

381
00:35:33.750 --> 00:35:35.750
It's good to meet you finally, Sébastien.

382
00:35:35.833 --> 00:35:38.917
- Do you mind if I call you Booker?
- Whichever you like.

383
00:35:41.708 --> 00:35:44.000
How long are you guys gonna keep this up?

384
00:35:44.083 --> 00:35:46.083
This whole cold shoulder bit. Hmm?

385
00:35:46.167 --> 00:35:48.833
How do we know
you haven't sold us out again, Book?

386
00:35:49.417 --> 00:35:50.750
Come on.

387
00:35:56.917 --> 00:35:58.167
Well, I, uh…

388
00:35:59.833 --> 00:36:01.083
I guess you don't.

389
00:37:26.000 --> 00:37:27.208
Andromache.

390
00:37:30.167 --> 00:37:32.083
This is not who you are.

391
00:37:49.833 --> 00:37:51.625
Woke up alone in the car.

392
00:37:53.083 --> 00:37:54.667
Thought you ditched me.

393
00:37:55.667 --> 00:37:56.875
Thought about it.

394
00:37:59.667 --> 00:38:01.208
Anything I can do?

395
00:38:04.917 --> 00:38:07.375
Can you give me back five centuries?

396
00:38:09.375 --> 00:38:10.625
Wish I could.

397
00:38:26.250 --> 00:38:28.250
What if she doesn't recognize me?

398
00:38:32.500 --> 00:38:34.375
I don't mean physically, but…

399
00:38:35.667 --> 00:38:37.083
Who I've become.

400
00:38:44.250 --> 00:38:46.208
What if I don't recognize her?

401
00:38:48.083 --> 00:38:50.792
Andy, I've never seen you like this.

402
00:38:59.792 --> 00:39:02.000
I've been like this for hundreds of years.

403
00:39:24.875 --> 00:39:26.458
I'll be right behind you.

404
00:39:29.917 --> 00:39:30.917
Okay.

405
00:40:06.375 --> 00:40:08.625
Excuse me,
can I use this phone for a second?

406
00:40:08.708 --> 00:40:09.708
Of course.

407
00:41:41.667 --> 00:41:43.125
I don't know how to…

408
00:41:46.792 --> 00:41:49.500
There are no words
to explain how I failed you.

409
00:41:58.875 --> 00:42:00.667
Can you imagine it?

410
00:42:02.083 --> 00:42:03.292
Trapped

411
00:42:04.333 --> 00:42:05.333
in the dark.

412
00:42:06.792 --> 00:42:08.708
Every muscle

413
00:42:09.208 --> 00:42:11.250
screaming for air.

414
00:42:13.000 --> 00:42:17.583
My life returning just long enough…

415
00:42:19.625 --> 00:42:21.208
To remember,

416
00:42:22.458 --> 00:42:23.458
to hope.

417
00:42:28.292 --> 00:42:29.750
I'm so sorry.

418
00:42:32.458 --> 00:42:34.000
I'm so sorry.

419
00:42:51.583 --> 00:42:53.250
How long have you been back?

420
00:42:54.375 --> 00:42:55.583
Months.

421
00:42:56.958 --> 00:42:58.708
Why didn't you come find me sooner?

422
00:42:58.792 --> 00:43:02.875
You couldn't even find me
in one small area of ocean.

423
00:43:03.542 --> 00:43:04.792
I searched.

424
00:43:05.875 --> 00:43:07.792
I did. I searched for centuries...

425
00:43:07.875 --> 00:43:09.250
But you stopped.

426
00:43:34.708 --> 00:43:35.708
Quynh.

427
00:43:40.250 --> 00:43:41.250
Look at me.

428
00:43:47.375 --> 00:43:49.125
You once told me…

429
00:43:51.500 --> 00:43:55.417
The only thing you fear is being alone.

430
00:43:59.083 --> 00:44:01.958
The way it was
before we found each other, Andromache.

431
00:44:05.208 --> 00:44:07.292
- I am alone.
- You're not.

432
00:44:07.375 --> 00:44:08.625
You have me.

433
00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:12.583
You have Joe and Nicky.

434
00:44:14.500 --> 00:44:15.500
Quynh.

435
00:44:18.875 --> 00:44:20.000
Come home.

436
00:44:21.208 --> 00:44:22.458
You can join us.

437
00:44:22.958 --> 00:44:25.625
You're asking me to join you

438
00:44:26.375 --> 00:44:28.250
and your endless war?

439
00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:30.125
Huh?

440
00:44:30.208 --> 00:44:31.917
Fight beside you?

441
00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:36.458
Fight for mortals, the ones who drowned me
in a coffin at the bottom of the sea?

442
00:44:36.958 --> 00:44:39.458
You have no idea

443
00:44:40.625 --> 00:44:41.833
what has happened.

444
00:44:45.167 --> 00:44:46.167
I can't…

445
00:44:48.083 --> 00:44:49.583
I can't leave them.

446
00:44:54.333 --> 00:44:55.375
I'm not…

447
00:44:59.625 --> 00:45:00.708
What?

448
00:45:07.292 --> 00:45:09.625
Looks like you have made your decision.

449
00:45:09.708 --> 00:45:10.708
Don't.

450
00:45:12.125 --> 00:45:13.583
Quynh, wait.

451
00:45:21.917 --> 00:45:23.292
Stay back.

452
00:45:50.083 --> 00:45:51.083
Quynh.

453
00:46:02.250 --> 00:46:04.167
Wait. I don't wanna fight.

454
00:46:40.833 --> 00:46:45.500
I remember the woman
I gave that necklace to a long time ago.

455
00:46:47.125 --> 00:46:48.625
And you're not her.

456
00:47:09.458 --> 00:47:10.542
Shit! Andy.

457
00:47:11.042 --> 00:47:12.042
Hey!

458
00:47:14.958 --> 00:47:16.375
Shut it down.

459
00:47:16.875 --> 00:47:18.417
Discord's here.

460
00:47:29.708 --> 00:47:31.833
Nile! No, no, no.

461
00:47:31.917 --> 00:47:33.042
That's Nile?

462
00:47:37.833 --> 00:47:39.500
What do you know about Nile?

463
00:47:44.667 --> 00:47:45.792
Discord.

464
00:47:46.958 --> 00:47:48.500
That's how you got out?

465
00:47:50.583 --> 00:47:51.958
You're with Discord.

466
00:48:00.292 --> 00:48:01.542
Stop!

467
00:48:02.583 --> 00:48:03.667
Stop.

468
00:48:15.458 --> 00:48:18.917
I curse you for all your lifetimes!

469
00:49:29.500 --> 00:49:32.333
Clever. Hiding in a church.

470
00:49:34.250 --> 00:49:36.250
But you can't stay here forever.

471
00:49:36.750 --> 00:49:38.667
I didn't think we'd be meeting so soon.

472
00:49:42.250 --> 00:49:43.750
I was there, you know.

473
00:49:44.792 --> 00:49:46.083
I can still remember it.

474
00:49:48.208 --> 00:49:50.833
The acrid stench of hate in the air.

475
00:49:54.667 --> 00:49:56.083
Tell me, Nile Freeman,

476
00:49:56.583 --> 00:50:00.708
how does a good Christian girl like you
stomach what Andromache's doing?

477
00:50:01.292 --> 00:50:03.583
Playing God with mankind.

478
00:50:04.167 --> 00:50:06.000
We're not playing God.

479
00:50:06.083 --> 00:50:08.750
We're helping. We're doing what's right.

480
00:50:09.292 --> 00:50:12.000
Did it feel right
leaving your family behind?

481
00:50:12.708 --> 00:50:14.458
Letting them think you were dead?

482
00:50:16.375 --> 00:50:18.125
That's what she made you do, isn't it?

483
00:50:18.208 --> 00:50:21.292
That was my decision, my choice.

484
00:50:22.083 --> 00:50:24.000
None of you had a choice.

485
00:50:24.625 --> 00:50:25.708
Not with her.

486
00:50:32.208 --> 00:50:35.667
Andromache's obsession
with interfering with human affairs

487
00:50:35.750 --> 00:50:38.125
is the reason we're hunted.

488
00:50:39.583 --> 00:50:42.000
You will make your friends stop

489
00:50:42.875 --> 00:50:43.958
or I will.

490
00:50:45.417 --> 00:50:48.042
You are the last immortal.

491
00:50:48.625 --> 00:50:50.833
There will be none born after you.

492
00:50:57.333 --> 00:51:00.583
And you have a power
you can't even imagine yet.

493
00:51:04.083 --> 00:51:05.958
One day you'll understand.

494
00:51:07.292 --> 00:51:11.417
You and I are going to end
immortal interference together.

495
00:51:12.500 --> 00:51:13.958
I'm not doing anything with you.

496
00:51:14.042 --> 00:51:15.750
We're connected.

497
00:51:16.708 --> 00:51:18.833
Do you have a birthmark on your left arm?

498
00:51:25.167 --> 00:51:26.417
The first immortal

499
00:51:27.250 --> 00:51:28.583
and the last.

500
00:51:29.458 --> 00:51:31.667
I'll see you soon, Nile.

501
00:51:57.208 --> 00:51:59.833
Clearly
Discord has the ability to find us.

502
00:52:01.125 --> 00:52:04.000
But now we have
all the surveillance footage from Rome.

503
00:52:04.083 --> 00:52:07.208
Next time Discord or Quynh
walks past a camera,

504
00:52:08.708 --> 00:52:09.917
we'll know where they are.

505
00:52:13.250 --> 00:52:15.250
- Well, that's something.
- What does it mean?

506
00:52:17.500 --> 00:52:18.625
"I'm the last."

507
00:52:20.292 --> 00:52:23.000
Discord knows
something about you we don't,

508
00:52:23.083 --> 00:52:25.125
and we need to figure it out.

509
00:52:25.667 --> 00:52:28.750
So what do we do about Quynh?

510
00:52:32.500 --> 00:52:33.500
I don't know.

511
00:53:33.708 --> 00:53:34.708
Booker.

512
00:53:35.167 --> 00:53:36.875
Are you working on something?

513
00:53:39.375 --> 00:53:40.417
Always.

514
00:53:45.917 --> 00:53:47.000
Tell me something.

515
00:53:49.458 --> 00:53:50.542
At any point,

516
00:53:51.583 --> 00:53:53.583
has Nile ever wounded Andy?

517
00:53:54.583 --> 00:53:56.917
Yeah. When they first met, they fought.

518
00:53:58.375 --> 00:54:00.417
Uh, Nile stabbed Andy.

519
00:54:02.667 --> 00:54:03.667
Why?

520
00:54:06.750 --> 00:54:08.083
Well, I, uh…

521
00:54:09.708 --> 00:54:14.083
I have a theory that that is the reason
why Andy has lost her immortality.

522
00:54:16.042 --> 00:54:17.667
What are you talking about?

523
00:54:18.792 --> 00:54:21.625
Any day, any one of us
could wake up mortal, right?

524
00:54:24.167 --> 00:54:26.625
Nothing that lives… lives forever.

525
00:54:33.167 --> 00:54:34.542
There was a legend

526
00:54:34.625 --> 00:54:37.750
that Discord and I had heard of
centuries ago.

527
00:54:39.083 --> 00:54:40.375
It tells

528
00:54:41.750 --> 00:54:44.625
that a wound from the last immortal

529
00:54:44.708 --> 00:54:49.250
has the power to take away
anyone else's immortality.

530
00:54:51.750 --> 00:54:54.458
So Nile is the reason Andy's mortal?

531
00:54:55.000 --> 00:54:56.000
Hmm.

532
00:54:57.292 --> 00:55:01.417
Well, I believe
that Discord is going to use Nile

533
00:55:01.500 --> 00:55:03.208
to try to kill all of us.

534
00:55:05.792 --> 00:55:06.958
But there's more.

535
00:55:07.042 --> 00:55:10.333
The legend also states
that the wounded immortal

536
00:55:10.417 --> 00:55:14.875
may bestow the gift of immortality
to another before it is lost.

537
00:55:19.375 --> 00:55:20.542
A transfer.

538
00:55:21.250 --> 00:55:22.417
Precisely.

539
00:55:23.917 --> 00:55:25.542
But it has to be willingly given.

540
00:55:28.458 --> 00:55:32.000
So Andy could… become immortal again?

541
00:55:34.708 --> 00:55:37.250
If one of us become mortal, yes.

542
00:55:40.083 --> 00:55:41.250
But again,

543
00:55:41.833 --> 00:55:43.208
it's just a theory.

544
00:55:51.000 --> 00:55:52.000
Andy?

545
00:55:52.917 --> 00:55:54.875
Can I talk to you for a sec?

546
00:55:54.958 --> 00:55:55.958
Sure.

547
00:56:01.583 --> 00:56:04.042
I just wanted to tell you,
after all of this is over,

548
00:56:04.125 --> 00:56:05.625
I'll probably go.

549
00:56:06.125 --> 00:56:08.625
Don't be stupid, Book. We need you.

550
00:56:09.917 --> 00:56:11.750
We never should have left you behind.

551
00:56:13.208 --> 00:56:14.917
You did what you had to do.

552
00:56:15.000 --> 00:56:16.458
I deserved it.

553
00:56:16.542 --> 00:56:17.542
Sit down.

554
00:56:20.042 --> 00:56:23.833
You remember the moment you left me?
You told me to have faith.

555
00:56:25.125 --> 00:56:26.125
Right?

556
00:56:27.292 --> 00:56:29.417
Well, the thing is, I, uh…

557
00:56:29.500 --> 00:56:30.542
I didn't,

558
00:56:31.375 --> 00:56:32.667
and it wrecked me.

559
00:56:34.042 --> 00:56:37.333
Seeing you walk away,
thinking I'd never see you again…

560
00:56:39.542 --> 00:56:41.458
Was, uh…

561
00:56:43.542 --> 00:56:47.750
But life is funny
'cause here I am talking to you.

562
00:56:49.208 --> 00:56:51.167
I'm really grateful for that.

563
00:56:53.792 --> 00:56:56.042
We've known each other too long.

564
00:56:57.125 --> 00:57:00.500
Yeah, so many things I left unsaid
all the time.

565
00:57:04.667 --> 00:57:07.333
When you get to do things
over and over again,

566
00:57:07.417 --> 00:57:10.083
forever, without expiration date, that's…

567
00:57:10.167 --> 00:57:13.042
That's where you forget
to say things to one another.

568
00:57:17.625 --> 00:57:19.792
I'd love an expiration date.

569
00:57:21.750 --> 00:57:22.833
You know why?

570
00:57:25.083 --> 00:57:26.833
'Cause it gives meaning.

571
00:57:30.875 --> 00:57:32.042
What I mean is,

572
00:57:32.125 --> 00:57:35.250
maybe this is the perfect time
for Quynh to be back.

573
00:57:41.750 --> 00:57:43.333
You wish for something

574
00:57:44.292 --> 00:57:45.625
for so long…

575
00:57:51.042 --> 00:57:52.833
But it's just not that simple.

576
00:57:53.417 --> 00:57:55.792
She's betraying you out of hurt.

577
00:57:58.375 --> 00:58:00.083
It's not over yet.

578
00:58:01.083 --> 00:58:03.042
We always make it through.

579
00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:07.583
Have a little faith, Andy.

580
00:58:11.250 --> 00:58:12.792
And get some sleep.

581
00:58:42.750 --> 00:58:44.125
She let you down again.

582
00:58:45.458 --> 00:58:46.583
I'm sorry.

583
00:58:53.333 --> 00:58:57.333
I pulled you from the ocean
because I needed you by my side.

584
00:58:58.667 --> 00:59:01.792
You may have lost Andromache,
but you don't have to be alone.

585
00:59:03.750 --> 00:59:05.250
How can I help you, Quynh?

586
00:59:07.083 --> 00:59:09.667
I want them to suffer.

587
00:59:11.458 --> 00:59:14.167
Andromache and the others, they will.

588
00:59:17.125 --> 00:59:18.125
No.

589
00:59:21.083 --> 00:59:22.500
Everyone.

590
00:59:25.083 --> 00:59:27.167
That I can help you with.

591
01:01:28.125 --> 01:01:29.250
Drop your weapons.

592
01:02:28.625 --> 01:02:30.083
Show me what you got.

593
01:02:34.333 --> 01:02:35.333
Really?

594
01:02:36.417 --> 01:02:37.667
Why not?

595
01:02:37.750 --> 01:02:39.833
I might be a couple of hundred years old,

596
01:02:39.917 --> 01:02:41.750
but I can still teach you a thing or two.

597
01:02:41.833 --> 01:02:44.250
Oh, you're gonna
teach me something? All right.

598
01:02:54.542 --> 01:02:56.208
Okay, Book.

599
01:02:58.167 --> 01:02:59.083
Hey, Tuah.

600
01:02:59.167 --> 01:03:01.708
You're just in time to watch me
school this old man.

601
01:03:01.792 --> 01:03:04.208
- Go easy on me. It's been a while.
- Mm-hmm.

602
01:03:04.292 --> 01:03:06.375
Perhaps you're not ready for this, Booker.

603
01:03:06.458 --> 01:03:07.458
All right.

604
01:03:17.667 --> 01:03:19.500
How am I doing, Tuah?

605
01:03:20.208 --> 01:03:21.625
You're a natural.

606
01:03:22.375 --> 01:03:23.708
I would like a chance too.

607
01:03:23.792 --> 01:03:26.292
Nah, let me play a little.

608
01:03:26.375 --> 01:03:27.625
I insist.

609
01:03:31.833 --> 01:03:32.833
All right.

610
01:04:06.542 --> 01:04:08.000
Shit.

611
01:04:08.083 --> 01:04:09.083
Argh!

612
01:04:09.167 --> 01:04:10.417
Sorry, Book.

613
01:04:10.500 --> 01:04:12.625
No, it's all right.

614
01:04:13.250 --> 01:04:15.042
That was fun.

615
01:04:19.083 --> 01:04:20.458
I'm gonna take care of this.

616
01:04:20.542 --> 01:04:21.625
All right.

617
01:04:22.792 --> 01:04:24.042
I'll be back.

618
01:04:30.542 --> 01:04:31.958
You shouldn't have done that.

619
01:04:33.667 --> 01:04:35.583
I told you it was just a theory.

620
01:04:35.667 --> 01:04:37.708
Only a theory.

621
01:04:38.583 --> 01:04:42.417
I can already tell.
It's… it's not healing.

622
01:04:47.208 --> 01:04:48.958
Then we don't have much time left.

623
01:04:50.250 --> 01:04:53.167
Remember, it must be given willingly.

624
01:04:56.542 --> 01:04:59.292
Tuah, you understand

625
01:04:59.375 --> 01:05:01.333
Andy can't know about this.

626
01:05:03.667 --> 01:05:04.792
She can't.

627
01:05:05.875 --> 01:05:07.000
Promise me.

628
01:05:20.917 --> 01:05:22.792
They're just outside Jakarta.

629
01:05:22.875 --> 01:05:25.042
We need to get everyone together
in the library.

630
01:05:25.542 --> 01:05:26.667
I'll be right there.

631
01:05:29.167 --> 01:05:31.125
You do something stupid again?

632
01:05:32.250 --> 01:05:33.958
Yeah, well, you know me.

633
01:05:34.542 --> 01:05:35.833
As usual.

634
01:05:37.500 --> 01:05:39.125
Copley wants us to meet downstairs.

635
01:05:40.125 --> 01:05:41.125
All right.

636
01:06:12.208 --> 01:06:13.333
You okay?

637
01:06:13.417 --> 01:06:15.000
Yeah.

638
01:06:15.083 --> 01:06:17.500
It's just been a while, you know.
It's not for me.

639
01:06:19.042 --> 01:06:20.625
Meet you downstairs.

640
01:06:34.542 --> 01:06:36.667
The nuclear facility is a black site.

641
01:06:37.417 --> 01:06:40.458
Privately owned by the Chinese
on Indonesian soil.

642
01:06:40.542 --> 01:06:41.958
It's not meant to exist.

643
01:06:42.500 --> 01:06:44.458
The confusion could be helpful.

644
01:06:44.958 --> 01:06:45.833
Yes.

645
01:06:45.917 --> 01:06:50.458
This is the security footage
that my contacts were able to obtain

646
01:06:50.542 --> 01:06:54.833
before all outside contact was cut off.

647
01:07:00.458 --> 01:07:03.208
We have to assume that her black ops team

648
01:07:03.292 --> 01:07:05.042
has full control of the system,

649
01:07:05.542 --> 01:07:07.625
from the control room
to the coolant chamber.

650
01:07:09.417 --> 01:07:11.000
Now, look at the large structure here.

651
01:07:11.500 --> 01:07:12.833
It's the core.

652
01:07:12.917 --> 01:07:14.833
It appears that, inside here,

653
01:07:14.917 --> 01:07:16.167
they've, uh,

654
01:07:17.167 --> 01:07:18.750
planted a device.

655
01:07:24.292 --> 01:07:28.083
We should assume that
it could create an explosion that would…

656
01:07:30.375 --> 01:07:31.500
Breach the facility.

657
01:07:31.583 --> 01:07:34.792
And irradiate the entire area.

658
01:07:34.875 --> 01:07:36.375
Ten million people.

659
01:07:37.667 --> 01:07:39.917
They've planted shaped charges

660
01:07:40.000 --> 01:07:43.167
capable of incapacitating any one of you

661
01:07:43.250 --> 01:07:47.083
for an extended
and vulnerable period of time.

662
01:07:47.750 --> 01:07:48.958
It's a trap.

663
01:07:49.542 --> 01:07:51.875
Discord is using the bomb like bait.

664
01:07:51.958 --> 01:07:56.083
She knows we'll try to stop her,
and we're playing right into her hands.

665
01:07:56.167 --> 01:07:57.958
That's exactly what she told me.

666
01:07:58.542 --> 01:08:00.042
She wants us.

667
01:08:01.250 --> 01:08:02.375
All of us.

668
01:08:04.167 --> 01:08:06.667
Whatever their motives are,
a bomb is a bomb.

669
01:08:06.750 --> 01:08:09.917
And both of them are willing to blow it
to get what they want.

670
01:08:11.958 --> 01:08:13.000
We don't have a choice.

671
01:08:14.292 --> 01:08:15.333
We have to go.

672
01:08:17.125 --> 01:08:18.125
Gear up.

673
01:08:29.833 --> 01:08:30.833
Thanks.

674
01:08:54.875 --> 01:08:58.583
Do you remember that game we used to play
in Ireland at the Cliffs of Moher?

675
01:09:00.125 --> 01:09:01.125
Yeah.

676
01:09:01.583 --> 01:09:03.042
Running towards the edge?

677
01:09:03.125 --> 01:09:06.125
See who chickens out first?

678
01:09:06.625 --> 01:09:08.000
You never gave up.

679
01:09:09.625 --> 01:09:10.708
No.

680
01:09:17.000 --> 01:09:18.042
Talk to me.

681
01:09:20.167 --> 01:09:22.042
I can't shake this fear, Nicky.

682
01:09:24.958 --> 01:09:26.375
And what are you afraid of?

683
01:09:29.500 --> 01:09:30.625
We could end.

684
01:09:34.167 --> 01:09:37.875
You know, Andromache,
she walks 3,000 years alone

685
01:09:37.958 --> 01:09:39.583
before she found Quynh.

686
01:09:41.500 --> 01:09:43.917
But me and you,
we were together from the start.

687
01:09:44.417 --> 01:09:48.250
I can't look at us
and believe it is arbitrary.

688
01:09:52.125 --> 01:09:53.292
Things end.

689
01:09:53.875 --> 01:09:56.500
What I feel when I see you,

690
01:09:58.042 --> 01:09:59.583
when I see your heart…

691
01:10:02.875 --> 01:10:04.417
That's truly immortal.

692
01:10:47.750 --> 01:10:49.833
<i>It would be ill-advised</i>

693
01:10:49.917 --> 01:10:52.792
<i>to discharge any firearm
in the vicinity of the core.</i>

694
01:10:53.708 --> 01:10:55.625
<i>James, negative contact.</i>

695
01:10:56.208 --> 01:10:58.625
Yeah, that means
you'll meet resistance further in.

696
01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:03.583
<i>Remember, we have to assume
they have our positions at all times.</i>

697
01:11:08.125 --> 01:11:09.792
Okay, doors on the south side.

698
01:11:10.708 --> 01:11:12.417
Through them, up the stairs.

699
01:11:22.167 --> 01:11:25.958
Stay along the wall and you're
in the upper levels of the reactor.

700
01:11:31.542 --> 01:11:32.583
<i>Any movement?</i>

701
01:11:33.167 --> 01:11:36.417
- Still nothing.
<i>- Joe, anything on your side?</i>

702
01:11:36.500 --> 01:11:38.625
<i>Negative contact on this side too.</i>

703
01:11:42.875 --> 01:11:43.917
Shaped charge.

704
01:11:46.875 --> 01:11:49.875
<i>Expect additional
small explosives throughout the compound.</i>

705
01:11:50.458 --> 01:11:54.083
Maybe they're not stupid enough
to stay in a nuclear facility,

706
01:11:54.167 --> 01:11:56.625
now that they've set a bomb to blow it up.

707
01:12:30.375 --> 01:12:32.708
<i>Okay, they wanna go hand-to-hand.</i>

708
01:12:33.292 --> 01:12:35.292
Remember, there's always an asshole.

709
01:12:44.583 --> 01:12:46.542
Go, go, go! Move!

710
01:13:28.000 --> 01:13:29.167
Nicky, get up!

711
01:13:41.375 --> 01:13:43.958
Get to the control room. Open that door.

712
01:13:49.375 --> 01:13:51.083
Copley, which way do we go?

713
01:13:51.167 --> 01:13:54.042
All right. Okay.
Down the hall, through the corridor.

714
01:13:54.125 --> 01:13:56.042
<i>It'll wrap around to the control room.</i>

715
01:14:33.583 --> 01:14:35.000
I found the asshole.

716
01:14:50.125 --> 01:14:52.417
Andy!

717
01:15:07.042 --> 01:15:08.167
Nile!

718
01:15:21.667 --> 01:15:22.958
Nile?

719
01:15:24.958 --> 01:15:27.542
<i>If I can get into their system,
I can lead you to the bomb.</i>

720
01:15:28.042 --> 01:15:29.250
<i>We haven't much time.</i>

721
01:15:35.125 --> 01:15:38.625
- The system has a firewall.
- <i>Look for a manual override.</i>

722
01:15:39.958 --> 01:15:41.583
There's no manual override, Copley.

723
01:15:52.167 --> 01:15:53.917
This was her plan all along.

724
01:15:54.000 --> 01:15:56.125
Discord wants to separate us.

725
01:16:11.542 --> 01:16:12.542
<i>Copley?</i>

726
01:16:46.417 --> 01:16:48.833
<i>Tuah? Nicky? Joe?</i>

727
01:16:48.917 --> 01:16:50.042
Nile.

728
01:17:11.042 --> 01:17:12.042
We're blocked.

729
01:17:12.083 --> 01:17:13.083
This way.

730
01:17:16.167 --> 01:17:18.000
Joe, Nicky, Nile!

731
01:17:18.500 --> 01:17:19.917
They're gone, Book.

732
01:17:20.500 --> 01:17:21.917
Discord is watching us.

733
01:17:27.500 --> 01:17:28.667
Let's go.

734
01:17:32.792 --> 01:17:36.208
She's controlling the doors.
She's trying to split us up.

735
01:17:38.583 --> 01:17:41.458
Book, when this door opens,
you have to go first.

736
01:17:41.542 --> 01:17:42.708
No, no, no. You go first.

737
01:17:42.792 --> 01:17:44.875
They're gonna slaughter me
if I go out there.

738
01:17:44.958 --> 01:17:45.875
You always go first.

739
01:17:45.958 --> 01:17:47.000
I'm not joking.

740
01:17:47.083 --> 01:17:48.375
Me neither, Andy.

741
01:17:51.292 --> 01:17:52.292
What?

742
01:17:52.792 --> 01:17:54.667
- I gave it to you.
- How?

743
01:17:55.625 --> 01:17:56.667
Stay behind me.

744
01:18:18.708 --> 01:18:21.125
I got my expiration date.

745
01:18:21.917 --> 01:18:23.833
You have a purpose.

746
01:18:25.750 --> 01:18:27.083
This is mine.

747
01:18:28.417 --> 01:18:29.542
Book!

748
01:18:32.542 --> 01:18:34.208
No! Book!

749
01:18:54.875 --> 01:18:56.000
No!

750
01:19:13.458 --> 01:19:15.125
Book!

751
01:19:27.833 --> 01:19:29.792
Book, I…

752
01:19:37.708 --> 01:19:39.042
Sébastien.

753
01:21:10.125 --> 01:21:11.125
You're alone.

754
01:21:12.250 --> 01:21:14.125
Give me the bomb, Quynh.

755
01:21:15.042 --> 01:21:16.458
Just go with Discord.

756
01:21:17.125 --> 01:21:18.542
Give her what she wants.

757
01:21:18.625 --> 01:21:20.375
She wants us dead.

758
01:21:22.583 --> 01:21:25.833
You stood with Andy for centuries.

759
01:21:26.333 --> 01:21:28.125
Centuries.

760
01:21:28.208 --> 01:21:30.833
How could you betray her like this?

761
01:21:37.625 --> 01:21:39.875
You know nothing about me and Andy.

762
01:22:12.083 --> 01:22:13.083
What…

763
01:22:20.125 --> 01:22:21.167
I'm not…

764
01:22:22.875 --> 01:22:23.875
I'm not healing.

765
01:22:24.417 --> 01:22:25.500
Quynh…

766
01:22:25.583 --> 01:22:27.208
What have you done to me?

767
01:22:27.292 --> 01:22:28.583
I didn't…

768
01:22:30.917 --> 01:22:32.458
I'm sorry.

769
01:22:39.625 --> 01:22:41.083
Shh.

770
01:22:41.167 --> 01:22:42.333
It's okay.

771
01:23:46.500 --> 01:23:48.792
Nile! Joe!

772
01:23:49.917 --> 01:23:51.000
Nicky!

773
01:23:51.792 --> 01:23:52.792
Tuah!

774
01:24:56.458 --> 01:24:59.708
Is this where you tell me
that this isn't who I am?

775
01:25:08.042 --> 01:25:10.250
I used to think it was my job to save you.

776
01:25:12.375 --> 01:25:13.667
But in the end,

777
01:25:14.667 --> 01:25:18.375
each one of us has to decide for ourselves
who we really are.

778
01:26:14.167 --> 01:26:15.917
Where is she taking them, Quynh?

779
01:26:17.750 --> 01:26:18.750
Where?

780
01:26:19.667 --> 01:26:20.750
I don't know.

781
01:26:31.333 --> 01:26:33.042
Bags loaded. Let's go!

782
01:28:44.750 --> 01:28:46.083
Circle around!

783
01:29:55.625 --> 01:29:56.917
Your hand isn't healing.

784
01:30:01.458 --> 01:30:02.458
You're mortal.

785
01:30:04.000 --> 01:30:07.417
This had nothing to do
with immortal interference, did it?

786
01:30:07.500 --> 01:30:09.042
Don't look at me like that.

787
01:30:10.167 --> 01:30:12.750
Do you know what it's like
to wake up after an eternity

788
01:30:12.833 --> 01:30:15.167
and find yourself suddenly mortal?

789
01:30:16.417 --> 01:30:18.375
Every minute

790
01:30:18.458 --> 01:30:20.583
is a step towards death.

791
01:30:21.250 --> 01:30:23.333
Time means nothing

792
01:30:24.417 --> 01:30:26.167
until it means everything.

793
01:30:26.250 --> 01:30:29.625
Time means nothing
if you give it no meaning.

794
01:30:34.458 --> 01:30:37.500
Your friends don't have
much time left, Andromache.

795
01:30:41.125 --> 01:30:42.417
That's your plan?

796
01:30:43.792 --> 01:30:44.958
You're gonna kill them?

797
01:30:45.458 --> 01:30:46.458
No.

798
01:30:47.750 --> 01:30:48.875
Nile will.

799
01:30:49.708 --> 01:30:51.375
She's a destroyer.

800
01:30:52.292 --> 01:30:54.542
She can take their immortality…

801
01:30:58.958 --> 01:31:00.500
<i>And give it to me.</i>

802
01:31:03.958 --> 01:31:05.208
She'll never hurt them.

803
01:31:06.458 --> 01:31:08.458
You think I'm gonna give her a choice?

804
01:31:19.958 --> 01:31:22.458
You think your life means more
than one of theirs?

805
01:31:23.292 --> 01:31:25.333
To me, it does.

806
01:31:26.750 --> 01:31:29.375
I suspect the first few won't be willing.

807
01:31:33.000 --> 01:31:34.167
And then again,

808
01:31:34.250 --> 01:31:37.000
torture goes a long way.

809
01:31:57.792 --> 01:32:00.000
I will come for them!

810
01:32:00.083 --> 01:32:03.583
And when you do,
the playing field will be level.

811
01:35:16.583 --> 01:35:20.583
There's a lot… I hate about this century,

812
01:35:21.208 --> 01:35:22.333
but this

813
01:35:23.125 --> 01:35:24.125
I like.

814
01:35:39.958 --> 01:35:42.417
I never knew Discord was mortal.

815
01:35:47.292 --> 01:35:48.708
I'm gonna find them.

816
01:35:50.625 --> 01:35:52.125
The only question is…

817
01:35:54.250 --> 01:35:57.250
Are you gonna do what you do best
and fight by my side?

818
01:36:00.875 --> 01:36:01.875
No.

819
01:36:09.500 --> 01:36:11.958
<i>You </i>will fight by <i>my </i>side.

820
01:36:17.833 --> 01:36:21.333
- Where do you think you're going?
- I always go first.

821
01:36:21.417 --> 01:36:23.375
Not anymore, you don't.

822
01:36:23.458 --> 01:36:24.500
Try and keep up.

823
01:36:24.583 --> 01:36:26.292
- Oh yeah?
- Yep.

824
01:36:37.917 --> 01:36:40.250
<i>I could feel it
I won't come down</i>

825
01:36:42.750 --> 01:36:46.208
<i>Found myself above the sky</i>

826
01:36:48.958 --> 01:36:53.167
<i>Tell my mama, tell my daddy</i>

827
01:36:55.333 --> 01:36:58.875
<i>That love is falling from the sky</i>

828
01:37:01.000 --> 01:37:03.833
<i>La, la, la-la, la-la</i>

829
01:37:07.458 --> 01:37:10.125
<i>La, la, la-la, la-la</i>
